{
 "$comment": "Cases for both theme checkers -- the reference in Go (tools/internal/formats, ParseTheme) and Clack's own in the browser (src/theme.ts) -- so the two cannot drift apart. Each of \"cases\" applies its edits to schema/examples/theme-annotated.json, read without its comments (a JSON Pointer to the value to set; null removes it; \"\" replaces the whole document), and says where the errors must be: one place, a list of places, or null for a theme that must be accepted. A refused case must have an error at each place and nowhere else. A theme is checked against the schema, then resolved onto the built-in it extends, then for contrast in each scheme it is shown in, each step only if the one before passed; a contrast error is at the place of the colour that falls short, in the theme as resolved. Each of \"raw\" is a whole file -- its text, its bytes in base64, or a file in the repository -- for what only shows in the text, and says whether it is accepted and, if not, where its errors are.",
